From 5d610b8d71c7ebe68cafb4ccacd8384d4355ffad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vaishnavi220506 <183067453+Vaishnavi220506@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:31:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] [Model][Qwen4Exp] Accept pipeline parallelism with the
 N-gram PLE

Upstream rejects PP>1 for this checkpoint: verify_and_update_config and
the model_state constructor raise NotImplementedError when PLE layers
exist. Upstream PR #56444 lifted the ban by carrying PLE input ids on
the pipeline handoff. Upstream #61016 later made the model runner keep
stage-local input ids on every stage for raw-token models, which
covers the same need: a live probe (2026-10-20, results.md) measured
wire vs stage-local ids byte-identical on 768/768 consecutive
real-traffic calls across all three non-first stages; only the
fabricated warmup steps differ, by construction.

Keep only the guard deletions: PLE layers read the runner argument,
and intermediate tensors never carry input ids (contract tests
included). Without this patch a PP+PLE boot dies at config validation.
